				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				24,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Build): Update .gitignore to exclude build artifacts while preserving executables\n\n- Restructures .gitignore rules to ignore all contents under /Target except specific build outputs\n- Preserves final executable artifacts in debug/release directories and Windows target bundles\n- Maintains platform-specific installer outputs (NSIS, MSI, AppImage) while ignoring intermediate files\n\nThis aligns with Land's focus on minimizing repository noise and ensuring only relevant build products are tracked. The changes support cross-platform packaging workflows in Tauri while preventing accidental inclusion of large temporary build files that could bloat the repository. The structure reflects Land's multi-target build approach for Windows and potential future platforms.",
			"SHA": "9e19fb4852ca010d18b2ae18ccaa8640ffd94cf4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-29T19:29:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				24,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(build): add initial .gitignore file\n\nAdds an empty .gitignore file to establish standard repository configuration patterns for the Land project. While currently empty, this file will serve as a centralized location to:\n- Exclude build artifacts (e.g., Tauri target directories, Node modules)\n- Ignore editor/IDE temporary files\n- Prevent accidental commits of environment-specific configs\n\nThis foundational setup aligns with Land's cross-platform architecture needs and establishes hygiene patterns critical for maintaining a clean workspace as development scales across Rust (Mountain), TypeScript (Sky/Cocoon), and multiple build systems.",
			"SHA": "a0b82539ab8825cbb21156193fa30fb079d3c5de"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-29T17:20:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠃⠀⠀⠀",
				23,
				6
			],
			"Message": "refactor(build): Replace binary module with structured build system\n\n- Remove legacy `Source/Binary` module in favor of new `Build` system under `Source/Build.rs`\n- Implement comprehensive build configuration management with logging (using `env_logger` and `colored`)\n- Add enhanced error handling with detailed error variants and `thiserror`\n- Introduce atomic file operations with `Guard` system for safe Cargo.toml/tauri.conf modifications\n- Improve CLI argument parsing with environment variable support for build parameters\n- Add semantic version/bundle ID generation with PascalCase conversion utilities\n- Configure optimized release builds in new `.cargo/config.toml` (LTO, strip symbols)\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Removes previous binary module - all build commands must now use new `Build` entrypoint\nRefs #123",
			"SHA": "3d73508e7d10c7026542523d2a69b9f9c669e03b"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1778683950232
}